WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.680
Now that we know Spider-Man is sticking around
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe thanks to

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:10.350
the new deal Sony, Disney, and Marvel reached
in September 2019, it's not totally unreasonable

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.340
to think that Spider-Man 3 may feature another
major Avenger.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:19.699
Well, according to an entirely unconfirmed
rumor published by We Got This Covered, that

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.540
idea might become reality.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.160
And by "unconfirmed rumor," we mean "internet
chatter."

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.680
And by "might become reality," we mean, "nobody
actually has any idea, but hey we can dream,

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.680
right?"

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.340
The outlet cites unnamed sources claiming
that the upcoming Spider-Man 3 will co-star

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:42.800
another prominent Avenger: Captain Marvel,
Doctor Strange, or Ms. Marvel whom we've yet

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.100
to meet on screen.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.420
Here's what we think.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.900
Let's break this rumor down by starting with
Captain Marvel.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.399
Save for that awesome Endgame scene where
Spidey handed over the Iron Infinity Gauntlet

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.600
to the Kree-powered Captain, Peter Parker
and Carol Danvers haven't spent much time

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.660
on-screen together.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.160
On the other hand, there is that end-credits
scene from Spider-Man: Far From Home that

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:08.160
featured Talos and Soren, the Skrull couple
who first appeared in Captain Marvel.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.220
If that mysterious scene was setting up some
sort of Skrull storyline for Spider-Man 3,

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.700
Captain Marvel will probably want to be involved
in one way or another.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.120
After all, she's basically their savior.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.400
"I'll help you find a home — finish what
Mar-Vell started."

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.440
Captain Marvel and Spider-Man are also the
strongest contenders to be the face of the

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:34.680
MCU now that Iron Man and Captain America
are out of the picture, so having them share

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.540
the screen in Spider-Man 3 could be Disney's
way of ushering in the new era of Marvel at

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.440
the movies.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:45.940
That said, Tom Holland and Brie Larson are
A-list actors with their own superhero franchises

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:50.230
to focus on so there's a pretty decent chance
that they'll stick to their own corners of

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:53.080
the MCU and never meet up on screen again.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.960
Strange is a Master of the Mystic Arts who
deals with metaphysical threats to our reality.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.880
Spider-Man is a friendly neighborhood hero
whose battles are very grounded.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.380
They're not exactly a perfect superhero match.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.100
That's why it's easy to forget that Spidey
and Strange have a history.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:15.160
They spent some time together during Avengers:
Infinity War, which saw Peter's idea saving

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:20.520
the Sorcerer Supreme from Ebony Maw and the
duo engaging in a bit of banter though we

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.200
can't say that Strange was overly friendly
toward Spidey.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.880
"Wh-what is he, your ward?"

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.460
"No.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.240
I'm Peter, by the way."

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.280
"Doctor Strange."

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.280
"Oh, you're using your made-up names…

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.220
Um, I'm Spider-Man, then."

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.660
Strange is also based in New York, like Spidey,
so the odds of the two of them bumping into

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.380
one another seems fairly high.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.780
On the flip side, though, the upcoming Doctor
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness is bringing

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:49.480
another Avenger into the Sorcerer Supreme's
world for a little crossover action: Elizabeth

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.300
Olsen's Scarlet Witch.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.520
The flick is set to launch in theaters on
May 7, 2021 just a few months before Spider-Man

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.980
3 opens on July 16, 2021.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.920
After watching Strange and Scarlet team up
in Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.350
audiences may have a "been there, done that"
attitude to Spider-Man 3 if it truly does

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.040
feature Doctor Strange.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.640
If the name "Ms. Marvel" isn't ringing any
bells for you, that's because the character

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.500
hasn't yet appeared on screen — but she
will.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:21.840
Kamala Khan, the Pakistani
American teenager who can stretch and bend

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.260
her body into all sorts of shapes, is confirmed
to star on her own upcoming series on the

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.260
new streaming service Disney+ a few years
from now.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:34.340
If Ms. Marvel doesn't premiere until 2022,
the character could first appear in Spider-Man

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.040
3.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.100
On one hand, Ms. Marvel debuting in Spider-Man
3 might make sense.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:44.400
Kamala is around the same age as Peter, and
since the MCU has no other teen heroes, it

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.760
would be great to see the two share the screen
together.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.340
On the other hand, it might be a horrible
decision.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.319
The House of Heroes rarely makes mistakes
when it comes to introducing characters into

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:58.520
its mammoth franchise that spans film and
now television, and having Kamala Khan take

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:03.040
her first turn on the screen in someone else's
movie could be a massive misstep that robs

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.180
the young hero of her own proper debut.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:19.860
Regardless of whether any of these Avengers
or any Avengers at all will join Peter Parker

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:25.669
in Spider-Man 3, Disney and Marvel clearly
don't plan on losing Spider-Man anytime soon.

00:04:25.669 --> 00:04:31.120
Spider-Man 3 could be one big Avengers reunion,
or it could be strictly centered around Spidey

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:31.940
himself.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:37.640
Either way, the film is sure to be a smash
when it swings into theaters on July 16, 2021.

